== Current candidate and release status ==
Reviewed October 24, 2026 for the page-owned candidate. The version, release date and stable status above identify the last tagged '''1.5.95''' release; they do not declare the candidate to be a stable Layers 2.0 release. Candidate registration/configuration and behavior are described below. Use an exact reviewed commit with passing CI and the [https://github.com/slickdexic/Layers/blob/codex/l01-publication-admission/docs/MILESTONE_1_RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md existing release checklist]. Editing this source file does not publish it to mediawiki.org.

The candidate stores layer sets in the '''owning page's native revision history''' after migration completion. A layer set belongs to one page and one file or slide. Equal names on different owners or files are independent. A PDF has one visible set name across all its pages; the page number selects an internal member, not a different set name.

Save publishes the complete owner snapshot in one native revision, preserving unrelated sets and complete PDF groups. Historical content retains its saved source identity. The old shared table and creator-based mutation APIs are separate legacy paths; shared writes become read-only after completion. The legacy null-edit history option is not needed for native history.

Use '''Edit layers''' and '''View full size''' on the saved embed, available on hover, keyboard focus or tap. Editing returns to the owning page. The old File-page tab is retired after completion. Ordinary embeds add no technical owner/revision headings or temporary set lists. Authors write names only, never owner page IDs or internal binding tokens.

Images and slides offer '''Download PNG''' first and a separate '''Download PDF'''. PDFs offer '''Download PDF''' only. Viewing, page navigation, Print and Download use the admitted saved content. Failed PDF pages must refuse complete assembly rather than silently shorten the result. OS/physical Print and the remaining device/version combinations retain their release-checklist limits.

== Why Layers? ==
* '''Professional Tools:''' 17 [[#Drawing Tools|drawing tools]], style presets, live preview, industry-standard alignment, a rich selection of [[#Annotation Tools|built-in shapes and emoji]], and '''[[#Slide Mode (v1.5.22+)|Slide Mode]]''' for standalone graphics.
* '''Non-Destructive:''' Original images are never modified. Annotations are stored separately and can be versioned or removed at any time.
* '''Accessible:''' Provides [[#Keyboard Shortcuts|keyboard controls]], ARIA labels, and high-contrast indicators. No formal WCAG conformance assessment is claimed.

