== Slide Mode (v1.5.22+) ==
A slide is a standalone canvas owned by the page whose snapshot contains it. Save the embed on that page, then use its overlay. The first argument selects the saved slide name. A migrated shared variant can be named <code>Safety overview (english)</code>; use its actual saved name without a page ID.

<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext">
[[File:Diagram.png|thumb|400px|layerset=ABC|Labels for this page]]
{{#Slide: Safety overview}}
{{#Slide: Safety overview|noedit}}
[[File:Manual.pdf|page=1|400px|layerset=001]]
[[File:Manual.pdf|page=2|400px|layerset=001]]
</syntaxhighlight>

After completion, <code>layerset=on</code> selects this owner/file's <code>Default</code> set, not the most recently saved shared set. <code>off</code> and <code>none</code> suppress layers; the older <code>layers=</code> spelling remains supported. Native names compare without case differences; spaces and underscores normalize alike, while the saved spelling remains visible. Missing sets may open empty for an eligible authorized editor, never by substituting another saved set.

Saved native geometry/background remain authoritative. Existing slide <code>size</code>/<code>noedit</code> syntax remains supported; verify the intended candidate result. Legacy shared-slide <code>layerset</code>, <code>canvas</code>, <code>background</code>, <code>size</code>, <code>class</code> and <code>editable</code> options, plus <code>Special:Slides</code>/<code>Special:EditSlide</code>, retain their separately labelled reference at [https://github.com/slickdexic/Layers/blob/codex/l01-publication-admission/wiki/Slide-Mode.md Slide Mode]. They do not grant admission to another page's native content. <code>noedit</code> hides an edit button, not server authorization.

== Installation and upgrade ==
The candidate's manifest requires MediaWiki 1.44 or newer. Use the PHP/database versions required by the chosen supported core release; the extension's compatibility floor is not an endorsement of an obsolete core version. See [https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Manual:Installation_requirements core installation requirements]. PDF layers require working native PDF thumbnails and the applicable media handler/rasterizer dependencies. Slides need no uploaded background file or PDF renderer.

For an older compatible 1.43 wiki, check the separate <code>REL1_43</code> branch and its actual fixes. <code>REL1_39</code> is unmaintained. Do not assume branch feature parity or mix PHP and assets from different branches. Shipped runtime assets are included; npm/Composer tools are for development checks, not a new extension runtime dependency.

From MediaWiki's <code>extensions</code> directory:
<syntaxhighlight lang="bash">
git clone https://github.com/slickdexic/Layers.git
git -C Layers checkout --detach REVIEWED_COMMIT_OR_TAG
</syntaxhighlight>
Replace the placeholder with the exact reviewed candidate/release and verify its CI. A default-branch clone or unchanged manifest number does not identify the candidate.

Add to <code>LocalSettings.php</code>:
<syntaxhighlight lang="php">
wfLoadExtension( 'Layers' );
</syntaxhighlight>
Then, from the MediaWiki root:
<syntaxhighlight lang="bash">
php maintenance/run.php update
</syntaxhighlight>

The updater is not migration completion. Follow the [https://github.com/slickdexic/Layers/blob/codex/l01-publication-admission/docs/UPGRADING.md full upgrade and recovery procedure]: rehearse on an actual wiki copy; retain consistent database/uploads/configuration backups and matching old code; arrange the edit freeze; refresh discovery; review the dry run; apply the unscoped migration; and verify <code>layerspagehistorymigrated: true</code> through siteinfo. A fresh empty wiki also needs completion recorded by that procedure. A scoped migration does not complete the whole wiki. Never fabricate the completion record or install a sample table manually.

Validate images, slides, complete PDFs, native history and current/old source versions before reopening normal edits. Retain shared rows and archived sources. Distinguish safe reruns, native content restoration and full backup rollback. A fresh successful migration does not automatically reconcile all earlier migrated history.

