Native document bounds are separate from legacy settings: 2097152 serialized bytes, 100 members, 100 layers per member, 1000 total layers and 4096-pixel canvas dimensions. Strict embedded-image validation permits at most 1048576 bytes for the complete image data URL, including base64 text. Raising a legacy setting does not expand these bounds or prune native page history.

New ownership defaults to content namespaces and File; an empty namespace array admits no new owners, while existing owners retain their content in any namespace, subject to permissions. The retired pilot-enabled/owner/namespace settings are ignored. Anonymous current-binding reads can remain cached for the configured age; historical, control, viewer/editor and private-wiki responses have stricter policies. Exact PDF delivery uses a separate no-store boundary.

See [https://github.com/slickdexic/Layers/blob/codex/l01-publication-admission/wiki/Configuration-Reference.md the configuration reference] for fonts, quotas, framing and per-path limits. The native registration/snapshot APIs are implemented; historical class names containing <code>Pilot</code> do not mean normal Saves still use shared storage.

=== Permissions ===
Native editing requires ordinary read/edit authority on the '''owning page''', <code>editlayers</code>, source visibility and fresh revision/source checks. Blocks and page protection apply. A File page and an article embedding its file are different owners. Save uses POST and native CSRF validation. A source listing, preview or old delivery descriptor is not lasting access or publication authority.

Registered users and sysops receive <code>editlayers</code> by default; anonymous users do not. Sysops receive <code>layers-admin</code> for legacy creator-check overrides. That right does not bypass native owner protection or source/revision visibility. Old shared rename/delete rules differ from native snapshot changes; earlier readable native revisions retain saved content. See [https://github.com/slickdexic/Layers/blob/codex/l01-publication-admission/wiki/Permissions.md permissions].

=== Maintenance and failure recovery ===
Keep unsaved work and drafts intact after an uncertain/refused Save. Use the existing '''Check'''/reconciliation flow to establish the outcome before republishing. Do not clear local storage, substitute another file/revision/PDF page or split native PDF Save into independent page writes.

The retained legacy renderer/export cache is separate from native history. Keep cached exports outside the document root and serve them through <code>Special:LayersExport</code>. To review derivative cleanup from the MediaWiki root:
<syntaxhighlight lang="bash">
php extensions/Layers/maintenance/purgeLayersRenderCache.php --max-age-days=30 --dry-run
</syntaxhighlight>
Review the reported cache paths before an intended cleanup. This is not a way to prune native revisions, legacy migration evidence, uploads or local acceptance archives. See [https://github.com/slickdexic/Layers/blob/codex/l01-publication-admission/wiki/Troubleshooting.md troubleshooting] and [https://github.com/slickdexic/Layers/blob/codex/l01-publication-admission/docs/KNOWN_ISSUES.md current limits].

== Key Features ==

=== Annotation Tools ===
* '''Callouts & Speech Bubbles''': Professional callouts with draggable tail positioning, three tail styles (triangle, curved, line), and rounded corners—perfect for tutorials and explanations.
* '''Curved Arrows''': Arrows support curved paths via a draggable control point, with configurable head types (arrow, circle, diamond, triangle) and line styles (solid, dashed, dotted).
* '''Text & Text Boxes''': Simple click-to-place text or advanced text boxes with word wrap, vertical alignment, padding, and corner radius.
* '''Shape Library (1,385 Shapes)''': Built-in library with 12 categories including arrows, basic shapes, callouts, flowchart, [[w:ISO 7010|ISO 7010]] safety symbols, [https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#iso:pub:PUB400008:en IEC 60417], ISO 7000, [[w:GHS hazard pictograms|GHS]], ECB, math, and more. All shapes render as crisp SVG vectors.
* '''Emoji Library (2,817 Emoji)''': Google Noto Color Emoji library with 19 categories (smileys, gestures, people, animals, food, travel, sports, and more). Lazy-loaded SVG thumbnails for fast browsing.

=== Visual Effects ===
* '''Blur Fill''': Apply a "frosted glass" blur effect to any shape—blur what's beneath instead of using a solid fill.
* '''Shadow & Glow''': Add drop shadows with configurable blur, offset, and spread. Glow effects for emphasis.
* '''Blend Modes''': Standard blend modes (multiply, screen, overlay, etc.) for professional compositing.
* '''Opacity Controls''': Independent fill and stroke opacity for fine-tuned transparency.

=== Layer Management ===
* '''Layer Folders''': Group layers into collapsible folders for organization. Visibility and lock states cascade to children.
* '''Named Layer Sets''': Keep several named layer sets for a file or slide within its owning page (e.g., "Default", "anatomy-labels", "step-by-step").
* '''Native Page History''': Successful page-owned changes are native owner-page revisions. Legacy shared retention settings do not prune native history; draft recovery remains local until Save succeeds.
* '''Lock & Visibility''': Lock layers to prevent accidental edits; toggle visibility for complex compositions.

=== Professional Workflow ===
* '''Style Presets''': Save and reuse style configurations (colors, stroke width, fonts) per tool type.
* '''Smart Guides''': Snap to edges and centers of other objects with visual alignment guides.
* '''Key Object Alignment''': Industry-standard alignment matching Adobe Illustrator—last selected object becomes the alignment anchor.
* '''Distribute Tools''': Evenly space selected layers horizontally or vertically.

=== Interactive editing ===
* '''Live Color Preview''': Canvas updates in real-time as colors are selected in the color picker.
* '''Saved Page Content''': Return to the owning page and reopen to verify a confirmed Save. Other already-open views may require a reload after unsaved work is preserved.
* '''Instant Feedback''': All property changes (stroke width, font size, opacity) update the canvas immediately.
* '''Overlay Actions''': Edit layers and View full size appear on hover, focus or tap; edit availability also follows owner/source authorization.

=== Integration ===
* '''PDF Markup''': Each PDF page is an internal member of one visible layer-set name and native owner snapshot. Use the standard <code>page=</code> option and editor page navigation. The '''View full size''' overlay opens the in-wiki viewer with bundled [https://mozilla.github.io/pdf.js/ pdf.js] (Apache-2.0, loaded on demand), admitted source and saved layers, plus paging, zoom, Print and Download. A plain browser PDF tab does not add Layers data. Working native PDF thumbnails/media-handler support is required, normally through {{ll|Extension:PdfHandler|PdfHandler}}.
* '''Import Images''': Add external images as layers (PNG, JPG, GIF, WebP).
* '''Export as PNG''': Download the annotated image as a single PNG file.
* '''Source Repositories''': Retained legacy foreign-file paths are separate from the native version-one snapshot contract, which captures local upload versions. Do not assume an unqualified foreign source is an admitted historical native source.
* '''Vector 2022 Dark Mode''': Supports MediaWiki's {{ll|Skin:Vector/2022|2=Vector 2022 skin}} night mode; qualify the intended skin/device and contrast behavior with the release matrix.

=== Galleries and existing Cargo helpers ===
Named layer sets work in galleries as well as inline file links.

'''Native <code><nowiki><gallery></nowiki></code> blocks (v1.5.75):'''
<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext">
<gallery mode="packed" widths=200>
File:Anatomy.jpg|layerset=anatomy|Anatomical labels
File:Physiology.jpg|layerset=physiology
</gallery>
</syntaxhighlight>

'''Existing Cargo <code>format=gallery</code> helper:''' The formatter accepts a <code>layerset</code> query-result field. The example preserves the existing interface; native row/occurrence behavior, including repeated files with different names, requires its applicable qualification and is not complete Cargo milestone acceptance:
<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext">
{{#cargo_query:tables=MyImages|fields=Image,layerset|format=gallery|mode=packed|image width=200}}
</syntaxhighlight>
If your column has a different name, add <code>layerset field=yourfield</code> to the query.

'''Manual hint registration (v1.5.73):''' For other gallery sources, call <code><nowiki>{{#layers_hint:Filename.jpg|setname}}</nowiki></code> before the gallery renders. Returns empty string (no visible output).

